idea by: @AlwaysRocket A tiny universe of 2,642 loose cubes. The only force is gravity – every cube pulling on every other cube. The biggest planet pulls hardest: a moon falls onto it, two moons crash head-on and rain down on it, a comet destroys the green planet and a meteor hits at 56,400 km/h. Each cube is read as a 100 km block of rock (the same physics works at any size); the clock shows the real time. Real rigid-body physics (Bullet), rendered in Blender.

@AlwaysRocket Thank you for the cool idea :)

#satisfyingvideo #satisfying #blender #blender3d #physics
